      "filename": "docs/design/arch_overview.md",
      "patch": "@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ This document provides an overview of the vLLM architecture.\n vLLM provides a number of entrypoints for interacting with the system. The\n following diagram shows the relationship between them.\n \n-![Entrypoints Diagram](../assets/design/arch_overview/entrypoints.excalidraw.png)\n+![Entrypoints diagram](../assets/design/arch_overview/entrypoints_v1.png)\n \n ### LLM Class\n \n@@ -133,40 +133,35 @@ For CPU resource sizing recommendations, see\n \n ## LLM Engine\n \n-The `LLMEngine` and `AsyncLLMEngine` classes are central to the functioning of\n-the vLLM system, handling model inference and asynchronous request processing.\n+The offline and online front ends prepare requests and process outputs. The\n+EngineCore schedules requests and manages the KV cache. The model executor\n+dispatches model work to GPU workers.\n \n-![LLMEngine Diagram](../assets/design/arch_overview/llm_engine.excalidraw.png)\n+![LLM Engine V1 diagram](../assets/design/arch_overview/llm_engine_v1.png)\n \n ### LLMEngine\n \n-The `LLMEngine` class is the core component of the vLLM engine. It is\n-responsible for receiving requests from clients and generating outputs from the\n-model. The `LLMEngine` includes input processing, model execution (possibly\n-distributed across multiple hosts and/or GPUs), scheduling, and output\n-processing.\n+The `LLM` class uses `LLMEngine` for offline inference. This V1 class is a\n+compatibility layer. The `LLMEngine` handles input and output processing. It prepares requests and converts EngineCore outputs to\n+`RequestOutput` objects. It sends requests to `EngineCore` through\n+`EngineCoreClient`. `EngineCore` then handles model execution (possibly distributed across multiple hosts and/or GPUs) and scheduling.\n \n-- **Input Processing**: Handles tokenization of input text using the specified\n-  tokenizer.\n-- **Scheduling**: Chooses which requests are processed in each step.\n-- **Model Execution**: Manages the execution of the language model, including\n-  distributed execution across multiple GPUs.\n-- **Output Processing**: Processes the outputs generated by the model, decoding the\n-  token IDs from a language model into human-readable text.\n+The code for `LLMEngine` is in\n+[vllm/v1/engine/llm_engine.py](../../vllm/v1/engine/llm_engine.py).\n \n-The code for `LLMEngine` can be found in [vllm/engine/llm_engine.py](../../vllm/engine/llm_engine.py).\n+### AsyncLLM\n \n-### AsyncLLMEngine\n+The API server uses `AsyncLLM` for online serving. `AsyncLLM` uses `asyncio` and\n+a background output handler to route EngineCore outputs to each request. Its\n+`generate()` method yields outputs to the API layer. `AsyncLLM` sends requests to\n+EngineCore through an asynchronous `EngineCoreClient`.\n \n-The `AsyncLLMEngine` class is an asynchronous wrapper for the `LLMEngine` class.\n-It uses `asyncio` to create a background loop that continuously processes\n-incoming requests. The `AsyncLLMEngine` is designed for online serving, where it\n-can handle multiple concurrent requests and stream outputs to clients.\n+`AsyncLLMEngine` remains a compatibility alias for `AsyncLLM`. The demo API\n+server uses this alias in\n+[examples/applications/api_server/server.py](../../examples/applications/api_server/server.py).\n \n-The OpenAI-compatible API server uses the `AsyncLLMEngine`. There is also a demo\n-API server that serves as a simpler example in [examples/applications/api_server/server.py](../../examples/applications/api_server/server.py).\n-\n-The code for `AsyncLLMEngine` can be found in [vllm/engine/async_llm_engine.py](../../vllm/engine/async_llm_engine.py).\n+The code for `AsyncLLM` is in\n+[vllm/v1/engine/async_llm.py](../../vllm/v1/engine/async_llm.py).\n \n ## Worker\n ",
